Devin, before you spend a morning in the budget file, three things about how =
it is built that are not obvious from the tabs.

The variance column compares the request against the current forecast rather =
than against last year's budget. That is deliberate and it is the comparison =
management uses, but it means a large variance often reflects a forecast chan=
ge rather than a spending change.

Second, several lines are marked approved with condition. The condition is in=
 the comment column and it is usually a release gate rather than a reduction.=
 Reading those as approved overstates the committed spend.

Third, the headcount-linked flag is set by account rather than by line, so a =
facilities line in an engineering cost centre reads as not headcount-linked e=
ven though it obviously scales with people.

Kip, this is the sort of thing worth writing into the file notes so the next =
person does not rediscover it.

